---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const toc = [
  { id: 'boundary', label: 'What REA does not do' },
  { id: 'pin', label: 'Pin' },
  { id: 'start', label: 'Start JEB yourself' },
  { id: 'ops', label: 'Operations' },
  { id: 'semantics', label: 'Semantics' },
  { id: 'steps', label: 'Operator steps' },
  { id: 'related', label: 'Related' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="JEB with REA 6.4.0 — bring your own license | rea.run"
  description="Operator guide for REA 6.4.0 JEB MCP: caller-started local engine, loopback URL, read-only tools. REA does not ship or launch JEB."
  path="/docs/jeb/"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12">
    <div class="docs-layout">
      <aside class="docs-toc hidden md:block">
        <p class="section-kicker mb-3">On this page</p>
        {toc.map((item) => <a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a>)}
      </aside>
      <article class="prose-page">
        <p class="text-sm"><a class="quiet-link" href="/docs/install/">← Install</a></p>
        <p class="badge badge-accent mt-4">Docs · 6.4.0</p>
        <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">JEB with REA (bring your own license)</h1>
        <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none">
          <code>rea-agents@6.4.0</code> can browse JEB project units and decompile a selected item through a <strong>JEB MCP server you already started</strong>.
          REA does not install JEB, does not launch it, and does not open <code>.jdb2</code> databases by itself.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Use a licensed JEB build on artifacts you are allowed to inspect.
          <a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a>
        </p>

        <h2 id="boundary">What REA does not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>It does not download JEB, patch a trial, or accept a license key.</li>
          <li>It does not start the GUI or a headless engine. You start MCP, then point REA at the loopback URL.</li>
          <li>Rename, comment, <code>save_project</code>, and <code>close_project</code> exist on the engine. REA 6.4.0 does not expose those mutation tools.</li>
          <li>An unreachable endpoint is a provider-availability failure. REA does not retry by spawning JEB.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="pin">Pin</h2>
        <p>Teaching and CI on this site use the npm release checked on 2026-10-13:</p>
        <pre><code>npx -y rea-agents@6.4.0 doctor --json</code></pre>
        <p>
          JEB support is a 6.4.0 highlight (<a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/1536" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1536</a>, published 2026-10-11).
          Upstream docs at tag <code>rea-agents-6.4.0</code> say the lane was checked against JEB <strong>5.48.0</strong> (Linux x64, licensed build) serving <code>jeb-mcp-server</code> <strong>1.3.0</strong> over streamable HTTP.
          Treat that as the upstream checkpoint, then confirm your own build with <code>inspect_jeb_client</code>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="start">Start JEB yourself</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Install JEB from the vendor with a license you hold. Put the client on the classpath if you use the programmatic route.</li>
          <li>In the GUI, start the MCP server from the File menu (or the vendor assistant the JEB docs name).</li>
          <li>Headless: use JEB’s documented <code>JebMcpServerInstance</code> API. Upstream notes that JEB 5.48’s <code>-c</code> headless mode does <strong>not</strong> accept <code>--mcp</code> directly.</li>
          <li>Default endpoint: <code>http://127.0.0.1:8425/mcp</code>. Override with <code>REA_JEB_MCP_URL</code>.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>The override must be an absolute <code>http</code> or <code>https</code> URL whose host is the literal <code>127.0.0.1</code> or <code>[::1]</code>. Redirects, remote hosts, credentials, query strings, and fragments are rejected. They are not stripped and reused.</p>
        <pre><code>export REA_JEB_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8425/mcp
npx -y rea-agents@6.4.0 doctor --json</code></pre>

        <h2 id="ops">Operations in 6.4.0</h2>
        <p>These four surfaces are read-only toward the target file. Only <code>open_jeb_project</code> changes engine-side project state. Evidence records the endpoint, the parameters you passed, and the digests the engine reports.</p>
        <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>MCP tool</th><th>CLI</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>inspect_jeb_client</code></td>
                <td><code>inspect-jeb-client</code></td>
                <td>Engine version, GUI or headless, startup time</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>open_jeb_project</code></td>
                <td><code>open-jeb-project</code></td>
                <td>Open or create a project from an artifact or <code>.jdb2</code> on the engine host. Returns SHA-256 of inputs and top-level units.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>list_jeb_units</code></td>
                <td><code>list-jeb-units</code></td>
                <td>Page units by stable path and type (<code>filter</code>, <code>parent-unit-path</code>, <code>index</code>, <code>count</code>)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>decompile_jeb_item</code></td>
                <td><code>decompile-jeb-item</code></td>
                <td>Decompile one type or method to the engine’s pseudo-code</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          <strong>Headless coverage (upstream, JEB 5.48.0).</strong>
          Headless MCP instances do not advertise <code>open_project</code>. Select the target when the engine client starts (<code>--infile</code> on the programmatic launcher, or open the file in the GUI).
          <code>open_jeb_project</code> completes only when the engine advertises the tool. REA keeps the engine’s refusal reason.
        </p>

        <h2 id="semantics">Semantics worth pinning in a runbook</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Paths in <code>open_jeb_project</code> are resolved by the <strong>JEB process</strong>, not by REA. The artifact does not have to exist on the REA machine.</li>
          <li>The engine caps <code>list_units</code> pages at 100. A full page is <code>coverage: "partial"</code> because more units may exist. An empty remainder is <code>complete</code> only when fewer units than requested came back.</li>
          <li>If <code>decompile_jeb_item</code> omits <code>unit_path</code>, the engine may pick the project’s first code unit. REA reports <code>unit_path: null</code> and a limitation. It does not guess the unit.</li>
          <li>Engine envelopes with <code>success: false</code> stay unsupported-target errors that carry the engine’s message (for example a missing item address).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="steps">Operator steps</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Confirm the target is yours, a debug build you produced, or another artifact you are allowed to open in a licensed decompiler.</li>
          <li>Pin <code>rea-agents@6.4.0</code>. Refresh MCP tool definitions after the pin. See the <a href="/docs/breaking/">6.0–6.4 upgrade runbook</a> if scripts still expect pre-6.2 Evidence wrappers.</li>
          <li>Start JEB MCP on loopback. Export <code>REA_JEB_MCP_URL</code> only if you moved the port.</li>
          <li>Call <code>inspect_jeb_client</code> and record version, mode, and the URL you used.</li>
          <li>Open the project through a GUI that advertises <code>open_project</code>, or start headless with the file already selected.</li>
          <li>Page units, then decompile one named item with an explicit <code>unit_path</code>.</li>
          <li>Keep the Evidence record. Do not paste pseudo-code from someone else’s commercial product into a public ticket.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Static Android work that does not need JEB stays on JADX. The Aegis study on this site is that path, pinned to the same package:
          <a href="/showcase/aegis-totp/">authenticator login-code case</a>.
          Device work is a different lane: <a href="/docs/android-adb/">Android ADB</a>, your emulator or device only.
        </p>

        <h2 id="related">Related</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/blog/rea-agents-6-4-0/">6.4.0 operator guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/android-adb/">Android ADB device lane</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/breaking/">Breaking changes 6.0–6.4.0</a></li>
          <li><a href="/faq/what-can-i-analyze/">Capability matrix</a></li>
          <li><a href="/faq/setup-vs-providers/">Setup does not install JEB</a></li>
        </ul>

        <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] pt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] not-prose">
          <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Sources</p>
          <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-xs">
            <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/rea-agents-6.4.0/docs/jeb-analysis.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">docs/jeb-analysis.md at rea-agents-6.4.0</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/releases/tag/rea-agents-6.4.0" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">rea-agents 6.4.0 release (2026-10-11)</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/pull/1536" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">#1536 — caller-started JEB MCP</a></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="mt-4"><a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></p>
        </footer>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
